<report>
<title>Simple linear regression</title>

<p><b>Equation: </b>@ytitle = @{slope:roundu} @xtitle @lnk @{abs_yintercept:roundu}</p>

<block name="se">
<p>Standard Error of slope = @{slope_err:roundu}<br />
<ci>@{se_pc:round2}% CI for population value of slope = @{se_from:roundu} to @{se_to:roundu}</ci></p>

<p>Correlation coefficient (r) = @{se_r:roundu} (r<sub>2</sub> = @{se_r2:roundu})</p>

<block name="ci">
<p><ci>@{ci_pc:round1}% CI for r (Fisher's z transformed) = @{ci_from:roundu} to @{ci_to:roundu}</ci></p>

<p>t with @df DF = @{tdf:roundu}<br />
<pval>Two sided @{p:pval}</pval><br />
Power @pwr</p>

<p>@sig</p>
</block>
</block>
<block name="notcalc">
<p><warn>SE and CI for slope not calculated when r = 1 or -1</warn><br />
<subtotal>Correlation coefficient (r) = @{r:roundu}</subtotal><br />
<warn>CI and t for correlation not calculated when r = 1 or -1</warn></p>
</block>
</report>
